From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:51:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: Let Settings set the PIHooks disable props

The Play Integrity Fix switch in Settings writes
persist.sys.pihooks.disable.gms_props, but only shell may set
pih_disable_prop. Settings runs as system_app, so the set is denied,
SystemProperties.set() throws and Settings crashes as soon as the
switch is turned on.
---
 sepolicy/private/system_app.te | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sepolicy/private/system_app.te b/sepolicy/private/system_app.te
index ac91c77..8db68f7 100644
--- a/sepolicy/private/system_app.te
+++ b/sepolicy/private/system_app.te
@@ -4,3 +4,6 @@ get_prop(system_app, aospa_build_prop)
 # Keystore compatibility
 allow system_app keystore_compat_data_file:dir create_dir_perms;
 allow system_app keystore_compat_data_file:file create_file_perms;
+
+# Play Integrity Fix: the switch in Settings sets persist.sys.pihooks.disable.*
+set_prop(system_app, pih_disable_prop)
-- 
2.55.0

